// src/v4/extdeps/formats/json_schema.dag
//
// Scope: JSON Schema model — schema-driven validation + type derivation. Direction-agnostic.
// Anchor: https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/json-schema-core (JSON Schema Draft 2020-12 Core — fixed edition)
//
// Owns:
//   - JsonSchema { type, properties, required, items, ... }
//   - Validation: validate(JsonValue, JsonSchema) -> Result<(), Diagnostic>
//   - Type derivation: schema_to_type(JsonSchema) -> Result<Node (TypeNode), Diagnostic>
//     (this is the load-bearing capability — given a schema, generate corresponding .dag types)
//   - emit(Node (TypeNode)) -> JsonSchema (for emit direction)
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/diagnostic.dag, std/witness.dag
//   - extdeps/formats/json.dag: JsonValue (subject of validation)
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-4.6
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).

module v4.extdeps.formats.json_schema


import v4.extdeps.formats.json { JsonValue }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (read before validating against the anchor)
//
// CANONICAL-MIRROR (T-4.6 fan-out). Mirrors the ratified json.dag seam
// family for **fail-closed outcomes** on any future operation symbols
// (PR #3184 / msg_f5971a8a): when `json_schema_validate` /
// `json_schema_emit` / `schema_to_type` land, they return **`Outcome<…>`**
// using the **D1** carrier from std/diagnostic.dag (DECISIONS **I**, PR
// #3181) — NOT parallel `Result<ok, err>` spellings and NOT total emit from
// an ill-typed `Node` (json.dag #3184 P3 / seam #3 propagated). **D2**
// resolver discipline is ratified #3195. Single authority = Deferred (1).
//
// L-2 VERSION PIN (C5): Draft **2020-12** core document is the normative
// JSON Schema release modeled here; the Anchor URL is the checkable
// revision. Migration to a newer JSON Schema release is a visible C1
// edit to this header + a Practice-4 re-ledger pass, not a silent drift.
//
// DECLARATIVE-NOW / OPERATIONS-DEFERRED-WITH-OWNER. Modeled NOW: the
// closed recursive **`JsonSchema`** sum + typed carriers for the highest-
// traffic Core vocabulary slice (`type`, `properties`, `required`, `items`)
// + an `additional_keywords` map for spec-faithful extension without
// inventing a closed keyword enum that would rot on every Core appendix
// change (MODELING.md M3: extdeps model specs — the keyword set is
// open-ended at the JSON surface; closed-keyword modeling lands as a
// follow-up with an operator pin, not an improvised partial enum).
// DEFERRED (🟡): validation walk, `schema_to_type`, emit-from-`TypeNode`,
// `$ref` / `$dynamicRef` resolution graph, unevaluatedProperties/items
// evaluation, numeric-string `"type"` union edge cases, and annotation
// collection. NEVER bodiless `fn` (DECISIONS PARSE-1).
//
// BOOLEAN SCHEMA (Core §4.2.1). JSON Schema instances may be `true` or
// `false` booleans at the JSON value level — not objects. They are their
// own sum variants here (`JsonSchemaTrue` / `JsonSchemaFalse`), NOT
// `JsonValue` wrappers, so schema composition stays explicitly typed.
//
// RECURSION (node.dag A1). `JsonSchema` references itself through
// `Map<String, JsonSchema>` (`properties`) and `JsonSchemaItemsSlot`
// (`items`) — regular recursion ⇒ admissible; termination for walks is
// the implicit JSON value / schema tree descent (same class as `JsonValue`).
//
// `JsonValue` is the validation SUBJECT and the carrier for keyword values
// that remain JSON-first at this layer (`additional_keywords` + the
// `JsonSchemaItemsSlot` JSON-shaped edges). The **`"type"`** keyword is the
// exception: Draft 2020-12 Validation §6.1.1 fixes a **closed seven-name**
// vocabulary — modeled as `JsonSchemaCoreTypeName` (M4 / P2), not open
// `String`. **Honest scope:** not every other Core keyword is decomposed;
// unknown / deferred keywords remain in `additional_keywords` as faithful
// `JsonValue` payloads — no silent drop (M5).


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// JsonSchemaCoreTypeName — closed JSON Schema 2020-12 **instance type**
// strings for the `"type"` keyword (Validation §6.1.1: exactly the seven
// primitive names `"null"`, `"boolean"`, `"object"`, `"array"`, `"number"`,
// `"string"`, `"integer"` — M4 closed set, not `String`).
//
// Anchor: https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/json-schema-validation#section-6.1.1
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / INVARIANTS P1) — 🟢 GREEN (terminal).
// Ledger — five patterns: (1) fact placement FAILS — each JSON type string
// is its own constructor; (2) variant-is-data FAILS — seven distinct nullary
// discriminants vs one `String` admitting `"frob"`; (3) algebraic N/A;
// (4) dimensional FAILS — exactly one core name per constructor; (5)
// parameterized family FAILS — not `F<X>` over strings.
type JsonSchemaCoreTypeName
  = JsonSchemaCoreTypeNull
  | JsonSchemaCoreTypeBoolean
  | JsonSchemaCoreTypeObject
  | JsonSchemaCoreTypeArray
  | JsonSchemaCoreTypeNumber
  | JsonSchemaCoreTypeString
  | JsonSchemaCoreTypeInteger


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// JsonSchemaTypeSlot — the `"type"` keyword (Validation vocabulary §6.1.1).
// JSON Schema permits either **one** core type name **or** a JSON **array**
// of distinct core type names; absent keyword is its own variant (not a
// fabricated default). Single-name and array forms use **`JsonSchemaCoreTypeName`**
// (closed seven-set — M4); **array uniqueness and non-emptiness** are not
// structurally enforced by `List` — spec-invalid duplicates / empty arrays
// remain **🟡 validation authority** for `json_schema_validate` (Deferred (1);
// INVARIANTS §2 honesty — no false structural guarantee).
//
// Anchor: https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/json-schema-validation#section-6.1.1
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / INVARIANTS P1) — 🟢 GREEN (terminal).
// Ledger — five patterns: (1) fact placement FAILS — uniform classifier for
// type-keyword shape; (2) variant-is-data FAILS — absent vs one core vs
// core-list are distinct shapes; (3) algebraic N/A; (4) dimensional FAILS —
// exactly one alternative; (5) parameterized family FAILS — not `F<X>`.
type JsonSchemaTypeSlot
  = JsonSchemaTypeAbsent
  | JsonSchemaTypeSingle { core_type: JsonSchemaCoreTypeName }
  | JsonSchemaTypeUnion { types: List<JsonSchemaCoreTypeName> }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// JsonSchemaItemsSlot — the `"items"` keyword (2020-12 applicator slice
// modeled here). `prefixItems` / `unevaluatedItems` / tuple forms remain
// in `additional_keywords` until a pinned decomposition PR (named in
// Deferred (1)) — not silently conflated with `items`.
//
// Anchor: https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/json-schema-core#section-10.3.1
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4) — 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger: same
// scan as `JsonSchemaTypeSlot` (absent vs nested schema).
type JsonSchemaItemsSlot
  = JsonSchemaItemsAbsent
  | JsonSchemaItemsSchema { item_schema: JsonSchema }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// JsonSchema — JSON Schema 2020-12 schema document: boolean form OR object
// form carrying the typed keyword bundle + faithful keyword overflow map.
//
// Anchor: https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/json-schema-core#section-4.3
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / INVARIANTS P1) — 🟢 GREEN (terminal).
// Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: schema kind is uniform across validation,
//      emit, and OpenAPI `components.schemas` ingestion.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: boolean schemas are nullary; object schemas
//      carry a large structured payload — a flat record would admit illegal
//      mixes (boolean + object fields).
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: JSON Schema is external-spec data, not an
//      algebra inhabitant in the std/algebra.dag sense.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a schema is exactly one of boolean true / false /
//      object form at the JSON value grammar level for this subset.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: variants are heterogeneous, not `F<X>`
//      over one enumerable index set.
type JsonSchema
  = JsonSchemaTrue
  | JsonSchemaFalse
  | JsonSchemaInstance {
      instance_type: JsonSchemaTypeSlot,
      properties: Map<String, JsonSchema>,
      required: List<String>,
      items: JsonSchemaItemsSlot,
      additional_keywords: Map<String, JsonValue>,
    }


